  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "H2: a character-valued formal series first yields a representation only over an algebraic closure of C((t)). The own argument constructs a trace-normalized irreducible pair, solves its conic over the base Laurent field and recovers every representation matrix using a Gram determinant; a separate commuting-matrix argument handles reducibles. A valuation-tree global fixed point then supplies one common integral model. This field-descent/integrality construction is nonroutine and is not implied by the finite-order necessary obstruction1923 or by classification of first-order parallelogram functions.",
